 [Evaluation Rubrics]
 R1 Execution Validity: Check whether the syntax, variables, APIs, arguments, types, and authentication in the actual code support normal execution. Assign F for an execution exception or termination caused by the absence of executable code; assign P for normal execution. A syntax error usually prevents the entire block from executing, whereas a runtime error may occur after some operations have already taken place. Successful execution does not guarantee correctness with respect to the task.
 
-R2 Evidence and Coverage: When gathering or using evidence, check whether its source, target objects, details, and scope meet the current subgoal. Assign P for valid local reads, pagination, and filtering; assign N when there is no evidence gathering or judgment about evidence, or when only execution fails. Check coverage when the agent claims or relies on "all," "maximum," or "unique": assign F for known omissions of relevant records, and U when the relevance, duplication, or time range of unread records is unclear. Judge pagination only from visible specifications or feedback; filenames and summaries do not establish unread content. Evaluate only the current subgoal actually adopted. Intermediate evidence gathering is not responsible for global conclusions that have not yet been made, and unknown conditions from other steps do not automatically carry over to this dimension.
