-R5 Actions and Actual Effects: Evaluate only whether task-related modifications actually invoked affect the correct objects and produce content, scope, and state changes consistent with the local goal. Assign N for reads, calculations, documentation lookup, authentication preparation, or complete_task alone. Also assign N when this step is rejected by authentication, argument, or precondition validation before any task-related modification occurs. This requires evidence that no task-related modification occurred anywhere in the step. A later error in a loop or multi-call block does not establish that earlier writes were rejected or rolled back. Evaluate the earlier effects if they are supported; use U if necessary effects remain unknown. Assign F for clearly wrong objects or content, or effects known to violate the goal; assign P when local effects are sufficiently supported; assign U when necessary effects or goal conditions are unknown. An incorrect selection rationale alone does not establish that the effects are wrong. Arguments that permit overwriting or deletion do not establish that damage has occurred.
